  "Question": "A group of 160 students is going on a visit. Each vehicle can seat at most 45 people. What is the minimum number of vehicles that must be rented?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "4",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Let \\(x\\) be the number of vehicles rented. Then \\(45x\\geq160\\), so \\(x\\geq3.56\\). Since \\(x\\) is an integer, at least 4 vehicles are needed.\n\nAlternative method 1: Account for the remaining students\n\nDivide the students into groups of at most 45:\n\\[\n160=45\\cdot3+25.\n\\]\nEven three full vehicles leave 25 students. One more vehicle holds those students because \\(25<45\\). Thus three or fewer vehicles cannot carry everyone, and four suffice, so the minimum is \\(4\\) vehicles.",
